---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Privacy Policy',href:'/privacy/'}];
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Talon Expeditions" description="Talon Expeditions privacy policy describing the information we collect, why we use it, how it may be shared, and the choices available to website visitors and travel customers." breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} noindex={false}>
  <section class="content-hero"><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Legal & privacy</p><h1 class="section-title">Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lead">This policy explains how {business.legalName} collects, uses, stores, and shares personal information when you visit our website, contact us, request travel planning, or participate in a trip we help coordinate.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="narrow legal-prose"><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 10, 2026</p><div class="legal-note">Travel planning can require more personal information than an ordinary website inquiry. We try to collect information when it becomes relevant rather than asking every visitor for every possible detail at the beginning.</div>
  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2><p>We may collect information you provide directly, including your name, email address, phone number, organization or group, travel interests, proposed dates, budget information, traveler preferences, rooming information, and messages you send to us. When you move from an inquiry into an actual trip, we may also need information such as legal names, dates of birth, passport details, citizenship, emergency contacts, dietary information, accessibility needs, insurance information, loyalty-program details, and activity-specific information required by a supplier or operator.</p><p>We may also receive technical information when you use the website, such as IP address, browser type, device information, pages viewed, referring pages, approximate location derived from network information, and cookie or analytics identifiers where those tools are enabled.</p>
  <h2>2. Why we use information</h2><p>We use personal information to respond to inquiries, evaluate trip fit, prepare proposals, coordinate bookings, communicate with travelers and organizers, support payments and documentation, provide customer service, improve our website and services, prevent fraud or abuse, comply with legal obligations, and keep records related to travel transactions.</p><p>Where marketing communications are used, we may use contact information to send relevant trip announcements, planning resources, or company updates. You can opt out of marketing communications at any time. Transactional or service communications related to an active inquiry or booking are different from marketing communications and may still be necessary.</p>
  <h2>3. Information shared with travel providers</h2><p>Travel cannot be delivered by Talon Expeditions alone. Depending on the itinerary, information may need to be shared with airlines, hotels, cruise lines, tour operators, destination-management companies, ground-transport providers, activity operators, guides, instructors, insurance providers, payment providers, technology vendors, or other suppliers involved in the trip. We share the information reasonably required for the requested service.</p><p>Those organizations may operate under their own privacy policies and may process information in countries with different privacy laws. A supplier may require information directly from the traveler rather than through Talon.</p>
  <h2>4. Sensitive travel information</h2><p>Some trips involve information that deserves additional care, including passport data, medical or accessibility information, dietary requirements, and emergency contacts. We request this information only when it is relevant to travel planning, safety, supplier requirements, or traveler support. Do not send highly sensitive documents through ordinary email unless requested and you are comfortable using that channel.</p>
  <h2>5. Cookies and analytics</h2><p>The website may use essential cookies needed for normal operation and, where enabled, analytics or similar technologies that help us understand site usage. See our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> for more detail. We do not sell personal information to advertisers.</p>
  <h2>6. Data retention</h2><p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose it was collected, including customer service, trip records, accounting, dispute handling, fraud prevention, and legal or regulatory obligations. Retention periods can differ depending on the type of information and the travel service involved.</p>
  <h2>7. Security</h2><p>We use reasonable administrative and technical measures intended to protect personal information. No website, email system, or internet transmission can be guaranteed completely secure. Travelers should use care when transmitting passports, payment information, medical information, or other sensitive documents.</p>
  <h2>8. Your choices and requests</h2><p>You may contact us to ask about personal information associated with you, request correction of inaccurate information, or ask that information be deleted where we are not required to retain it. Rights can vary by location and may be subject to legal, contractual, or operational limitations.</p>
  <h2>9. Children</h2><p>Our public website is not directed to children. Group trips may include minors when arranged by parents, guardians, schools, clubs, or organizations. Information about a minor should be provided only by an authorized parent, guardian, or responsible organization and only when relevant to the trip.</p>
  <h2>10. Contact</h2><p>Privacy questions can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>. Written correspondence may be sent to {business.legalName}, {business.address.street}, {business.address.city}, {business.address.region} {business.address.postalCode}, United States.</p>
  <h2>11. Policy updates</h2><p>We may update this policy when our services, technology, suppliers, or legal obligations change. The effective date at the top of the page identifies the current published version.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
